        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: bound GitHub release and Discord gateway metadata response reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes potential unbounded response body reads in two places:\n- `src/agents/utils/tools-manager.ts` called `response.json()` on the GitHub releases API without a byte cap.\n- `extensions/discord/src/monitor/gateway-metadata.ts` called `response.text()` on the Discord `/gateway/bot` response without a byte cap.\n\nEither endpoint returning an unexpectedly large payload could cause the process to run out of memory.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReuses the existing shared helpers (`readResponseWithLimit` / `readDiscordGatewayMetadataBody`) to enforce the same byte limits that are already used on sibling bounded-read paths. For Discord, the existing `fetchDiscordGatewayMetadataGuarded` already materialized the body under the same cap; this change makes the direct `fetchDiscordGatewayInfo` path equally bounded.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change under normal operation. OpenClaw is now protected from accidental or hostile oversized JSON/text responses when checking GitHub tool releases or Discord gateway metadata.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal validation on `fix/response-bounding-tools-manager-discord`:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-oxlint.mjs \\\n  src/agents/utils/tools-manager.ts \\\n  extensions/discord/src/monitor/gateway-metadata.ts\n\nnpx oxfmt --check --threads=1 \\\n  src/agents/utils/tools-manager.ts \\\n  extensions/discord/src/monitor/gateway-metadata.ts\n\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.json --noEmit\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p extensions/discord/tsconfig.json --noEmit\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/agents/utils/tools-manager.test.ts \\\n  extensions/discord/src/monitor/gateway-metadata.test.ts\n```\n\n- Lint / format check: passed.\n- Core and Discord type-check: passed.\n- Focused tests: **12 passed** (`tools-manager` 8, `gateway-metadata` 4).\n\nCI on the latest push (`260cc6b0c2`) is fully green, including:\n- `Real behavior proof` ✅\n- `actionlint` ✅\n- `Security High (actions)` ✅\n- All changed-path test shards ✅\n\nThe `Real behavior proof` job covers the new loopback-server regression tests:\n- `tools-manager.test.ts` rejects an oversized GitHub release body.\n- `gateway-metadata.test.ts` rejects oversized bodies for both the guarded and direct Discord gateway metadata paths.\n\nAlso addressed the ClawSweeper review note about the `DiscordGatewayFetch` contract: it now returns `Promise<Response>` instead of a minimal `ok/status/text` shape, so the bounded reader no longer relies on an unsafe cast.",
